  "behavior_change": "Adds one independently gated, opt-in boot argument, rgpuvcnpreset=1, effective only when the existing rgpuvcnnodpm capability-alignment gate also holds (vcnNoDpmEnabled && ppCompatibilityBypassed), so it patches in the same video process at the same moment as the existing VCN DPM COW target. It adds three current-task copy-on-write byte patches to AMDRadeonVADriver2.bundle (UUID 81DF7215-43E2-3BA1-BE2D-EFB1C508B81A), sharing that image's existing identity check: (1) Vcn3EncCommand::addPresetEncodeModePacket (TEXT+0x4d458, 14 bytes) replaces the load of the encode preset from [rdi+0x30] (always 0) and its range check with an unconditional mov esi,0x01000007 plus a 9-byte NOP, so the function always tail-calls addPacket(this, 0x01000007, 0, 0) -- RENCODE_IB_OP_SET_BALANCE_ENCODING_MODE, Mesa radeonsi's HEVC default; (2) Vcn3EncHevcCommand::buildGeneralCommand (TEXT+0x4dd74, 8 bytes) and (3) Vcn3EncAvcCommand::buildGeneralCommand (TEXT+0x4d88c, 8 bytes) each nop the 2-byte jnz in `cmp byte [r12+0x1c],1; jnz +0xb` that otherwise skips the call to addPresetEncodeModePacket, since that flag is never set by the plugin, making the call unconditional. Each site goes through the same guarded path as the existing VCN DPM patch: exact instruction-byte match, UUID match, null-terminated path match, single RX page, task-private copy-on-write remap, write, protection restore, and read-back verification, with a sampled critical log per target (VCNPRESET: COW ... / VCNPRESET: image ...). Nothing else changes: no other boot argument, patch site, or code path is touched.",
